From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Hold each JSON string value at its own length

JSON.parse grew each string value one character at a time, and each
growth rounded up to the next power of two, so a value kept up to twice
the room it needed for as long as the parse's result lived. The shell
keeps its daemons' answers parsed, and in its weigh lab these values
were the largest holder of its malloc memory: 17.3 MB of 84.1 MB live.
No escape reads as more characters than it's written in, so the span to
the closing quote is room enough, and each value now reserves it first.

---
--- a/src/qml/jsruntime/qv4jsonobject.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/jsruntime/qv4jsonobject.cpp
@@ -562,6 +562,18 @@
 {
     BEGIN << "parse string stringPos=" << json;
 
+    // Grown a character at a time, a value was held at the next power of two
+    // of what it needed, up to twice that, for as long as the parse's result
+    // lived. No escape reads as more characters than it's written in, so the
+    // span to the closing quote is room enough for the whole value.
+    const QChar *close = json;
+    while (close < end && *close != u'"') {
+        if (*close == u'\\' && close + 1 < end)
+            ++close;
+        ++close;
+    }
+    string->reserve(close - json);
+
     while (json < end) {
         if (*json == u'"')
             break;
